# The image builds from the monorepo root (every workspace package ships TypeScript source with
# no build step, so Vite has to compile them in place) -- which means `COPY . .` pulls in the
# whole tree. Everything below either bloats the build context or must never reach an image.

.git
.github
.husky

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Local build output. Stale `dist` copied over a fresh build would serve yesterday's bundle.
**/dist
**/dist2
.turbo
**/.turbo
.tanstack
**/.tanstack

# Gitignored, and real: these hold live environment the developer last pointed at. 
# The container writes its own config.json at startup
# from environment variables (docker/10-runtime-config.sh) -- baking one in would both leak that
# environment's config and defeat the build-once/promote-many model.
apps/*/public/config.json
.env
.env.*

# Agent and editor context, never needed to build.
.devcontainer
.claude
.agents
.vscode
docs
CONTEXT-MAP.md
**/CONTEXT.md
**/*.md